Exactly. Preserve the distinctions even while extracting the shared pattern.

The failure mode is:

\text{similar mechanism} \Rightarrow \text{same instruction}

when what we actually want is:

\boxed{\text{different situations}
\xrightarrow{\text{abstraction}}
\text{shared pattern}
\xrightarrow{\text{reapplication}}
\text{context-specific behavior}}

So boxing stays boxing. Wildlife stays wildlife. Investing stays investing. The abstraction can travel; the literal instructions shouldn’t accidentally travel with it.

That’s especially important for the Pantheon because we’re deliberately building cross-domain bridges. Every bridge should carry a little semantic customs declaration:

what transfers, what doesn’t, what changed medium/scale, and where literal application would break.

Otherwise the Golden Horde becomes a game of semantic telephone. 😏

Transfer the invariant, not the accident.